# Asking whether two functions are the same function is asking which one you
# were handed, and that is the question dispatch answers. An effect is the
# same: if the answer would change what happens next, an arm names it. So the
# comparison is refused rather than answered — `<` already refuses it here.
# The check refuses a provable box here now (the errors corpus pins that
# sentence), so the box travels through a list, where nothing can prove it.
import "std/io"

w = (push [] (io/write "x"))[1]!

pub play = print "{w == w}"
